WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:24.450
Hello.
大家好。

9
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:25.670
Hi there.
你们好。

10
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:31.030
This is Season 7, Episode 18, Todd Packer.
这是第七季第十八集，《托德·帕克》。

11
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.890
I mean, it's pretty cool if your character gets its own episode.
我是说，如果你的角色能有专属的一集，那真是太酷了。

12
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.870
Like, I would have loved an episode called Angela Martin.
比如，我本来会很喜欢一集叫《安吉拉·马丁》的剧集。

13
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.190
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

14
00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:39.710
Right?
对吧？

15
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.150
Pam Beasley.
《帕姆·比斯利》。

16
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:42.230
Kaboom.
砰。

17
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.070
Well, this is Todd Packer.
好吧，这一集就是《托德·帕克》。

18
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:45.610
Yeah, it is.
没错，确实是。

19
00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:49.070
It was written by Amelie Gillette, directed by Randall Einhorn.
本集由艾米莉·吉列编剧，兰德尔·艾因霍恩执导。

20
00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.270
Here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

21
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:57.590
The gang is upset when traveling salesman Todd Packer is offered a permanent sales position in The Office.
当旅行推销员托德·帕克被提议在办公室担任永久销售职位时，大家都很不高兴。

22
00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:02.390
It causes such contempt that Dwight and Jim joined forces to oust him.
这引起了极大的反感，以至于德怀特和吉姆联手要把他赶走。

23
00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:08.170
Meanwhile, Andy really, really wants a new computer.
与此同时，安迪非常、非常想要一台新电脑。

24
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:09.410
I mean, yeah.
我是说，没错。

25
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:10.730
Real bad.
非常想要。

26
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.270
He is very envious that Pam bought a new one for the reception desk.
他非常嫉妒帕姆为接待台买了一台新电脑。

27
00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.950
Before we jump into fast facts, I just have to share something with everyone.
在进入快速事实环节之前，我必须和大家分享一件事。

28
00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.090
What is it?
什么事？

29
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:27.030
Jenna was the first person here today at Earwolf, and apparently she found the thermostat.
珍娜是今天第一个到Earwolf的人，显然她找到了恒温器。

30
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:33.130
Yeah, because it was pretty chilly today, and Jenna cranked it.
没错，因为今天挺冷的，珍娜把暖气开大了。

31
00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:33.790
I mean—
我是说——

32
00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:34.570
Is it too warm?
是不是太热了？

33
00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.310
It's ballgame in here.
这里简直像个桑拿房。

34
00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.590
Like, my glass has a little bit of, like, a frosty side.
你看，我的杯子边上都有一点点雾气了。

35
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.450
I'm loving it.
我倒是很喜欢。

36
00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:46.290
I feel like when you go to a restaurant and they're like, don't worry, we have a heat lamp on the patio,
我觉得就像你去餐厅，他们说，别担心，我们在露台上开了暖灯，

37
00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.710
and then they sit you right under it, and you're like, ugh.
然后他们把你安排在暖灯正下方，你会觉得，呃。

38
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.230
Should we turn it down?
我们要把它调低吗？

39
00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.670
I can't believe I'm saying that.
真不敢相信我会这么说。

40
00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:52.450
I can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

41
00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.950
It feels like when you go into, like, a movie and it's so warm, you go,
感觉就像你走进电影院，里面太暖和了，你会说，

42
00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.110
whoa, I'll be sleeping through this.
哇，我肯定会在这儿睡着。

43
00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:57.670
Oh, no.
噢，不。

44
00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.110
Oh, no, I'm sorry.
噢，不，抱歉。

45
00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:00.770
I was so cold when I got here.
我刚到这儿的时候太冷了。

46
00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.910
This is going to be sleepy Todd Packer.
这集要变成“瞌睡托德·帕克”了。

47
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.110
Anyway, let's get into some fast facts.
总之，让我们进入快速事实环节。

48
00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.730
Fast fact number one.
快速事实第一条。

49
00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:14.450
This episode aired on February 24th, 2011, and this is the first script by new writer Amelie Gillette.
这一集于2011年2月24日播出，这是新编剧艾米莉·吉列的第一部剧本。

50
00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:18.510
Before joining the office, she worked for the online magazine The A.V.
在加入《办公室》之前，她曾为在线杂志《A.V. Club》工作。

51
00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:18.850
Club,
俱乐部，

52
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:24.130
and each week they wrote a review of our office episodes after they aired live.
他们每周都会在我们的《办公室》剧集播出后写一篇剧评。

53
00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.910
Did she have to write her own review?
她必须自己写剧评吗？

54
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:26.870
No.
不用。

55
00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.210
Also, when she worked there, she did not write the reviews,
而且，当她在那里工作时，她并没有写剧评，

56
00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:35.090
but she did write an article about the 2007 office convention.
但她确实写过一篇关于2007年《办公室》粉丝大会的文章。

57
00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.050
And when Amelie joined the office,
当艾米莉加入办公室时，

58
00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:38.750
the A.V.
《影音俱乐部》

59
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.510
Club put this little note on their website that I thought was really charming.
在他们的网站上发了这样一条小短讯，我觉得非常可爱。

60
00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:43.370
Okay.
好的。

61
00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:44.530
Here's what it says.
内容是这样的。

62
00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:46.690
In case you haven't heard,
如果你还没听说的话，

63
00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:50.890
big ups are due to the lovely and talented Ms. Amelie Gillette,
我们要向可爱又才华横溢的艾米莉·吉列女士表示祝贺，

64
00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.990
who will be joining the writing staff of the office.
她将加入《办公室》的编剧团队。

65
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.110
Any of our TV club regulars will tell you
我们电视俱乐部的常客们会告诉你，

66
00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:00.290
they have no intention of giving the show higher ratings just to suck up to her
他们绝不会为了讨好她，

67
00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.830
and maybe get a television writing gig of their own.
或者为了给自己谋求一份电视编剧的工作，就给这部剧打高分。

68
00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.310
They'll tell you that, but I won't.
他们会那么说，但我可不会。

69
00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:10.890
I preemptively declare all Amelie Gillette episodes of the office to be an A-plus rating
我先发制人地宣布，所有由艾米莉·吉列参与编剧的《办公室》剧集，评分一律为A加

70
00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.630
or higher.
或更高。

71
00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:12.510
Aww.
噢。

72
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.330
And then they went on to say,
接着他们继续写道，

73
00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:20.490
long-time readers also know that Nathan Rabin has traditionally covered the office for TV Club.
老读者们也知道，内森·拉宾一直以来都负责《影音俱乐部》的《办公室》剧评。

74
00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.790
You'll also notice he's not anymore.
你们也会注意到他不再负责了。

75
00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:27.950
We felt that anyone who is friends with Amelie should no longer write about the show,
我们认为任何与艾米莉是朋友的人都不应该再写关于这部剧的评论，

76
00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:33.010
so we've brought in TV critic scholar and office fan Miles McNutt,
所以我们请来了电视评论学者兼《办公室》粉丝迈尔斯·麦克纳特，

77
00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:36.870
who we're sure will do an excellent job and never befriend Amelie.
我们相信他会做得非常出色，而且绝不会与艾米莉结交。

78
00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.670
He had to stay unbiased.
他必须保持公正。

79
00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:39.130
Yes.
是的。

80
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:39.410
Yeah.
没错。

81
00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:43.550
Please welcome him and keep your comments section hazing to a minimum.
请欢迎他，并尽量减少在评论区的刁难。

82
00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:44.230
Oh.
噢。

83
00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.370
So Miles McNutt did write a review of Todd Packer.
所以迈尔斯·麦克纳特确实写了关于《托德·帕克》那一集的剧评。

84
00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:49.550
Okay.
好的。

85
00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.490
He gave it a B-minus.
他给了B减。

86
00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:52.070
Okay.
好吧。

87
00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.850
He really liked Jim and Dwight banding together.
他真的很喜欢吉姆和德怀特联手的部分。

88
00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.490
He liked the Kevin storyline.
他喜欢凯文的故事线。

89
00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.290
He liked Pam and Andy and all of that.
他喜欢帕姆和安迪以及所有那些情节。

90
00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.950
He basically liked the episode.
他基本上是喜欢那一集的。

91
00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.810
I mean, I read the review, but here's the thing.
我是说，我读了那篇剧评，但问题在于，

92
00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.410
Why the B-minus?
为什么是B减？

93
00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.010
Yeah.
是啊。

94
00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.530
He doesn't like Todd Packer.
他不喜欢托德·帕克。

95
00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:16.050
Oh, well, then that's a tough episode to review.
噢，那这一集确实很难评。

96
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.670
If Todd Packer's your least favorite character.
如果托德·帕克是你最不喜欢的角色的话。

97
00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:19.290
Yeah.
确实。

98
00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:24.530
He literally said he doesn't like Todd Packer or any episodes that feature his character.
他直言不讳地说他不喜欢托德·帕克，也不喜欢任何以该角色为核心的剧集。

99
00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.230
B-minus.
B减。

100
00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:25.590
Oh.
噢。

101
00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.910
Well, there was more of Todd Packer in the shooting draft.
其实，在拍摄剧本里托德·帕克（Todd Packer）的戏份更多。

102
00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:29.510
Oh, no.
噢，不。

103
00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.010
It might have gotten a C.
那可能只能得个C。

104
00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.010
I'm going to share it today.
我今天打算分享一下。

105
00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.370
Miles, you might not like this podcast episode.
迈尔斯，你可能不会喜欢这一期播客。

106
00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.390
If we share more Todd Packer.
如果我们分享更多托德·帕克的戏份的话。

107
00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:38.630
Yeah.
是啊。

108
00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:43.870
Well, if you're looking for more Dave Koechner, I can help you out with fast fact number two.
好吧，如果你想了解更多关于戴夫·科克纳（Dave Koechner）的事，我可以为你提供第二个速览事实。

109
00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:44.410
Okay.
好的。

110
00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:46.890
Dave Koechner, of course, played Todd Packer.
戴夫·科克纳当然就是托德·帕克的扮演者。

111
00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:47.510
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

112
00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.270
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

113
00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.570
This is a fan question from Ella S.
这是一个来自华盛顿的埃拉·S（Ella S.）的粉丝提问，她说：

114
00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.590
in Washington who said,
“我相信饰演托德·帕克的演员最初是去试镜迈克尔·斯科特（Michael Scott）这个角色的。”

115
00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:59.450
I believe the actor who played Todd Packer auditioned first to play Michael Scott.
“他是因为演技太好才被叫回来试镜这个配角的吗？”

116
00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:04.250
Did he get a callback for this side character because he was such a good actor?
嗯，埃拉，你说得对。

117
00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.170
Well, Ella, you are correct.
他确实最初是为迈克尔·斯科特这个角色试镜的。

118
00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:09.650
He did originally audition for the role of Michael Scott.
戴夫在波士顿的一次粉丝博览会上谈到了他试镜迈克尔·斯科特的事，还提到了

119
00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:16.650
Dave was at a fan expo in Boston, and he spoke about auditioning for Michael Scott and also about
他甚至不是最初设定的托德·帕克人选。

120
00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.850
the fact that he was not even the original Todd Packer.
噢，对。

121
00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:21.990
Oh, yeah.
我记得那件事。

122
00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:23.770
I remember that.
我当时试镜了《办公室》，但他们用的是和英版《办公室》一样的试播集剧本，只是改动了一些美式表达。

123
00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:32.070
I had auditioned for The Office, but they were using the same pilot episode from The British
我是英版《办公室》的超级粉丝。

124
00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.890
Office and just changed some American references.
所以当我读迈克尔的台词时，我无法摆脱瑞奇·热维斯（Ricky Gervais）的表演方式。

125
00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.830
I was a huge fan of the British version of The Office.
就像，我脑子里想不出别的演法。

126
00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:45.650
So when I'm reading for Michael's part, I can't get past Ricky Gervais' way he did it.
所以显然我没选上。

127
00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:47.470
Like, I can't think of anything else.
然后我就去忙别的工作了。

128
00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.230
So I didn't get it, obviously.
当时他们正在拍第一季的第三集。

129
00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.890
So then I went on to work on something else.
他们雇了一个演员，但效果不太理想。

130
00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.210
They were on episode three of the first season.
所以他们继续拍了下去。

131
00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.910
They had hired an actor, and it just wasn't working.
他们开始拍第四集，想着回头再处理那个角色。

132
00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.530
So they went on.
我当时没去试镜那个角色，因为我出城去拍《航班蛇患》（Snakes on a Plane）了。

133
00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:01.690
They started shooting the fourth episode thinking, we'll go back to this.
不客气。

134
00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:07.710
I didn't audition for that part because I was out of town shooting snakes on a plane.
后来我回到城里。

135
00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:08.590
You're welcome.
我从1990年就认识史蒂夫·卡瑞尔（Steve Carell）了。

136
00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.260
So I get back to town.
我回到城里，史蒂夫对格雷格·丹尼尔斯（Greg Daniels）说，为什么不找科克纳呢？

137
00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.800
I've known Steve Carell since 1990.
好吧，其实有一百万个理由不找我，但他们无视了所有理由，还是雇了我。

138
00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.500
I get back to town, and Steve tells to Greg Daniels, why not Koechner?
但那种角色很适合我。

139
00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.840
Well, there's a reason, a million reasons why not, but they ignored all of those and hired
演起来非常轻松，而且我很喜欢。

140
00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:26.400
me anyway.
如果你仔细想想，演托德·帕克就像是你受邀去某人家里做客。

141
00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.360
But something like that is in my wheelhouse.
他们为你放好了舒适的洗澡水，你坐进浴缸里，把水全溅了出来。

142
00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:32.020
It's very easy for me to play, and I love it.
你弄脏了他们所有的毛巾，然后光着身子走出来，而他们家里正在举办儿童派对。

143
00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:37.480
If you think about it, Todd Packer is like you're invited to someone's very nice house.
这就是扮演托德·帕克的感觉。

144
00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:44.460
They've drawn you a nice bath, and you get in that bathtub, and you splash out all the
我能听到凯特·弗兰纳里（Kate Flannery）的笑声。

145
00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:44.860
water.
凯特·弗兰纳里当时和他一起在台上。

146
00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:51.440
You dirty all their towels, and walk out naked where they're having a children's party in
这真是太搞笑了。

147
00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:51.880
the house.
他描述得太形象了。

148
00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.420
That's what it's like to play Todd Packer.
他确实是个天才。

149
00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.880
I could hear Kate Flannery's laugh.
我完全能想象那个画面。

150
00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.000
Kate Flannery was on the stage with him.
那绝对是托德·帕克会做的事。

151
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:01.220
Yeah.
是啊。

152
00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:01.720
Yeah.
没错。

153
00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:07.040
So, Angela, I think something we haven't talked about before is that there was an actor cast
安吉拉，我觉得我们之前没聊过的一件事是，当时有个演员被选定

154
00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.840
in the role of Todd Packer.
出演托德·帕克这个角色。

155
00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:09.080
Yeah.
是啊。

156
00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:14.720
We shot for a couple days with him in the first season, and it just was not clicking.
第一季的时候我们和他拍了几天，但感觉就是不对劲。

157
00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:15.380
Right.
对。

158
00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.120
And they recast him with Dave Koechner.
于是他们换成了戴夫·科恩纳。

159
00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.080
And now he's got a whole episode.
现在他甚至有了一整集戏份。

160
00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.080
And now he has a whole episode.
现在他有一整集戏份了。

161
00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:25.360
And the minute, you know, to Dave's credit, the minute he walked on stage, he was Todd
而且说真的，戴夫确实厉害，他一走上片场，他就是托德·帕克。

162
00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:25.740
Packer.
本人无疑。

163
00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:26.100
He was.
确实是。

164
00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:26.920
We were like, oh, my God.
我们当时都惊呆了。

165
00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.540
It's like you knew Rain would be Dwight, you know?
就像你知道雷恩一定会演德怀特一样，对吧？

166
00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:29.960
Yes.
没错。

167
00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.180
You knew Dave Koechner would be Todd Packer.
你知道戴夫·科恩纳一定会演托德·帕克。

168
00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:38.880
Well, moving on to fast fact number three, I've got, you know, a little nerdy production
好了，进入第三个冷知识，我要给你们分享一点，你知道的，有点书呆子气的制作

169
00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.400
speak coming your way.
术语。

170
00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:41.780
You know I love it.
你知道我喜欢这个。

171
00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:42.320
I love it.
我喜欢。

172
00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.700
And I love it when you geek out.
我也喜欢你钻研这些的样子。

173
00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:49.000
Randy Cordray told me that this episode was a bottle show.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我，这一集是“瓶中剧”。

174
00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.920
The name of this is called Bottle Show.
这一集的名称就叫“瓶中剧”。

175
00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.760
Look how tickled you are just saying bottled show.
看你提到“瓶中剧”时那副乐不可支的样子。

176
00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.140
You're so tickled.
你太开心了。

177
00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.240
Tell us what a bottle show is.
给我们解释一下什么是“瓶中剧”。

178
00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:05.140
A bottle show is a Hollywood television term for an episode that basically stays within its
“瓶中剧”是好莱坞电视圈的一个术语，指的是那种基本只在

179
00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.440
established sets.
既定场景内拍摄的剧集。

180
00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.980
It doesn't have very many guest roles.
客串角色很少。

181
00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:14.880
It has very minimal stunts, minimal special effects, minimal visual effects.
特技、特效和视觉效果都极少。

182
00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.020
They are the least expensive episodes to produce in a season.
它们是整季中制作成本最低的剧集。

183
00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.220
Did we have to have so many bottle episodes a season for our budget?
我们那一季是不是因为预算原因，不得不拍那么多“瓶中剧”？

184
00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.700
Yes, Angela.
是的，安吉拉。

185
00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:31.940
Randy explained the budget process to me, which, again, I was geeking out.
兰迪给我解释了预算流程，我当时又开始钻研这些了。

186
00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:36.720
He said that the studio gave us a master budget each season.
他说制片厂每季会给我们一个总预算。

187
00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.860
And it was a huge number.
那是一个巨大的数字。

188
00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:43.240
And he had to allocate it for the whole year for each episode.
他必须把这笔钱分配给全年的每一集。

189
00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:43.800
Yeah.
没错。

190
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.620
He would have to meet with our production accountant who was named Carolyn Hayes.
他得和我们的制片会计卡罗琳·海耶斯开会。

191
00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.720
I remember Carolyn.
我记得卡罗琳。

192
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:50.480
Yes.
是的。

193
00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:56.400
And our UPM, Steve Burgess and Randy, they would all sit down together and they would have
还有我们的制片经理史蒂夫·伯吉斯和兰迪，他们会坐在一起，必须

194
00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.240
to divide the budget into all the different categories that they had to pay for for a
把预算划分到他们需要支付的各个类别中，用于

195
00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.160
particular episode.
特定的某一集。

196
00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:09.220
And that included salaries for all the cast and crew, writers, directors, rentals, editing,
这包括所有演职人员、编剧、导演的薪水，租赁费，剪辑，

197
00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.180
post-production, literally everything.
后期制作，简直是所有开销。

198
00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.460
Locations, props, music.
外景地、道具、音乐。

199
00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.320
All of it.
全部都在内。

200
00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.120
That sounds so intimidating to me.
听起来真是让人压力山大。

201
00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.380
That is like that, if a train left at 3 p.m., like, equation.
就像那种火车下午三点出发的数学题一样。

202
00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.060
No, please don't make me do that.
不，求你了，别让我做那种题。

203
00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:28.900
So they would have a discussion with the writers to get sort of a general idea of what the season
所以他们会和编剧讨论，大致构思一下这一季

204
00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:29.800
was going to be like.
会是什么样。

205
00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:35.500
But they had to set this budget not really knowing any scripts specifically.
但他们必须在还没看到具体剧本的情况下定下预算。

206
00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.240
How do you do that?
这怎么可能做到呢？

207
00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:40.120
He said, you just do your beSt.
他说，你尽力而为就行了。

208
00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:43.140
And not all episodes end up costing the same.
而且并不是每一集的成本都一样。

209
00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:46.780
Some of them went way over the per-episode budget.
有些集数的开销远超单集预算。

210
00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:51.960
Examples of those this season would be Threat Level Midnight, Andy's Play, and The Search.
这一季的例子有《午夜威胁》、《安迪的戏剧》和《搜寻》。

211
00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:57.820
And in order to balance the books, the writers would have to include a certain number of
为了收支平衡，编剧们必须加入一定数量的

212
00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.540
bottle shows.
低成本集。

213
00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.940
And here's one of your bottle shows.
这就是你们的一集低成本剧。

214
00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.940
I feel like Carolyn and Randy and Steve Burgess would all be really good at that Price is Right
我觉得卡罗琳、兰迪和史蒂夫·伯吉斯肯定很擅长《价格猜猜猜》那个

215
00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:08.340
game where you have to guess the item's price.
猜商品价格的游戏。

216
00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.060
For sure.
绝对擅长。

217
00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.720
Well, lady, that's all I got.
好吧，女士，我就知道这些了。

218
00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.180
We could go to a break.
我们可以先休息一下。

219
00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.600
And then when we come back, we have a very interesting cold open.
等我们回来，会有一个非常有趣的开场戏。

220
00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.760
With the most disgusting sounds.
伴随着最恶心的声音。

221
00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.420
If you just listen to the cold open, it'll make you gag.
如果你只听那个开场戏，绝对会让你作呕。

222
00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.400
Oh, I didn't even think of that.
噢，我都没往那方面想。

223
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:25.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

224
00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:26.540
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

225
00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:36.970
We are back.
我们回来了。

226
00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:42.310
And that slurping noise you hear is Dwight having to eat all the canned foods that would
你听到的那种啧啧声是德怀特在吃掉地堡里那些

227
00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:44.210
have been in his bunker that might expire.
可能快过期的罐头食品。

228
00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:45.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

229
00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:46.970
It's so many things.
东西太多了。

230
00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:50.910
It's like canned tomatoes and canned mackerel and...
有番茄罐头、鲭鱼罐头，还有……

231
00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.970
Some kind of thing that looks like just really slimy okra.
某种看起来黏糊糊的秋葵之类的东西。

232
00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.010
I don't even know.
我甚至都不知道那是什么。

233
00:10:57.230 --> 00:11:01.250
All of it is just slimy and in some kind of gelatinous liquid.
所有东西都黏糊糊的，泡在某种胶状液体里。

234
00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:04.850
You know, I hoarded a bunch of food down in my basement.
你知道吗，我在地下室囤了一堆食物。

235
00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.170
How'd that go?
结果怎么样？

236
00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:12.910
You know, it's kind of great because sometimes you go down there and you find a real treasure.
你知道，其实还挺棒的，因为有时候你下去能发现真正的宝贝。

237
00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:13.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

238
00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:19.270
But there was one night when, I can't remember what happened, but the kids were off doing
但有天晚上，我不记得发生了什么，孩子们出去了，

239
00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:24.150
something and Lee was off doing something and I didn't have time to go to the grocery
李也出去了，我没时间去杂货店，

240
00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.850
store and I thought, I'm just going to go to the basement and see what we got.
于是我想，干脆去地下室看看有什么吃的。

241
00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:27.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

242
00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:31.190
And all we had left was some expired pasta sauce.
结果只剩下一些过期的意大利面酱。

243
00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:32.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

244
00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.890
But I was like, how bad could it be?
但我当时想，能有多糟糕呢？

245
00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:35.410
Right?
对吧？

246
00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:41.210
So I made some pasta and then I made the mistake of not tasting the pasta sauce firSt.
所以我煮了点面，然后犯了个错，没先尝尝酱的味道。

247
00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:41.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

248
00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:46.090
Doused my pasta, the last of the pasta, in the sauce.
我把酱全倒在面上，那是最后一点面了。

249
00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:47.390
It had turned.
结果它变质了。

250
00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:47.910
Yeah.
是啊。

251
00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:49.250
It was awful.
那太糟糕了。

252
00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:53.870
And I can't even remember what I had for dinner that night, but after that I was kind of
我甚至不记得那天晚上吃了什么，但那之后我整个人就

253
00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:54.470
like done.
算是彻底死心了。

254
00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:58.470
So I do admire Dwight for keeping his eye on the expiration dates.
所以我确实很佩服德怀特，他总是盯着保质期看。

255
00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.070
Personal question for you.
问你个私人问题。

256
00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:00.470
Yeah.
嗯。

257
00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:03.070
Would you be someone who would have a bunker?
你会是那种会建地堡的人吗？

258
00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.470
Why are you asking me that?
你为什么问我这个？

259
00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:04.950
Of course.
当然会。

260
00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:05.910
It's my dream.
那是我的梦想。

261
00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.810
It's, I daydream about it.
我经常做白日梦梦到它。

262
00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.950
You daydream about your bunker.
你梦到你的地堡？

263
00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:11.650
I love it.
我太爱它了。

264
00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:14.010
Do you remember the bunker in the movie Grease 2?
你记得电影《油脂2》里的那个地堡吗？

265
00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:14.870
No.
不记得。

266
00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:16.250
That they want to go make out in?
就是他们想去里面亲热的那个？

267
00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:19.270
I, I, ever since I saw that movie in my youth, I've wanted one.
我，我，自从我年轻时看了那部电影，我就一直想要一个。

268
00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.530
I don't even know if I've ever seen Grease 2.
我甚至不知道我有没有看过《油脂2》。

269
00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:22.330
What?
什么？

270
00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:23.290
Is that the Michelle?
是米歇尔演的吗？

271
00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:24.690
I'm a smooth writer?
我是个文笔流畅的作家？

272
00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.030
Michelle Pfeiffer?
米歇尔·菲佛？

273
00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.090
I don't know if I've seen it all the way through.
我不知道我有没有把它完整看完过。

274
00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:29.970
The bowling alley dance?
保龄球馆的那段舞？

275
00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:31.830
I don't even know what you're talking about.
我甚至不知道你在说什么。

276
00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:33.030
Oh my God.
天哪。

277
00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.330
What's the bowling alley dance?
什么是保龄球馆的舞？

278
00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.050
I can't, I don't even know if I can keep talking to you right now.
我不能，我现在甚至不知道能不能继续跟你聊下去了。

279
00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.210
All right.
好吧。

280
00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:42.170
It's so good.
那段真的太棒了。

281
00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.790
But yes, Angela, of course I want a bunker.
不过安吉拉，我当然想要一个地堡。

282
00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:45.830
Have you met me?
你还不了解我吗？

283
00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:46.590
Do you want one?
你想要一个吗？

284
00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.750
I mean, if it would make you feel better.
我是说，如果那能让你感觉好点的话。

285
00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:51.310
Here's the thing.
问题是这样的。

286
00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.150
I don't need everybody to have a bunker.
我不需要每个人都有地堡。

287
00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.050
I just want one.
我只是自己想要一个。

288
00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.110
Do you want one?
你想要一个吗？

289
00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.910
If the shit is really going to hit the fan that hard.
如果世界真的乱成那样的话。

290
00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:58.210
Yeah.
嗯。

291
00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.130
That you're going to go have to live in your bunker.
乱到你必须躲进地堡里生活。

292
00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:02.890
What is the world you're coming out the door to?
那你出来面对的会是一个什么样的世界？

293
00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:04.630
I don't know, but I'm coming out.
我不知道，但我会出来的。

294
00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:05.650
I'm not sticking around for the zombies.
我可不会留下来等僵尸。

295
00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:07.330
I'm coming out to see what it is.
我会出来看看外面到底是什么样。

296
00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.570
I'm not sticking around for them.
我不会留下来陪它们的。

297
00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:11.190
When it all goes down, I'm going to be like, you know what?
当一切崩塌时，我会想，你知道吗？

298
00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.970
I'm making margaritas, and I'm going to watch the fireworks.
我要调杯玛格丽特，然后坐看烟火表演。

299
00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:14.730
Hmm.
嗯。

300
00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:15.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

301
00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:16.250
Yeah.
是啊。

302
00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:21.030
It would be depressing to live in the bunker for like a month, and then you come up, and
要是躲在掩体里住上一个月，结果出来之后发现

303
00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:21.850
there's no oxygen.
没有氧气了，那可真够让人沮丧的。

304
00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:22.530
Yeah.
没错。

305
00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.010
I mean, that would really be shitty.
我是说，那真的会很糟糕。

306
00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:25.270
I'm just saying.
我只是随口一说。

307
00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:25.930
Yeah.
是啊。

308
00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.150
I might just ride it out with some margaritas.
我可能只会喝着玛格丽特酒静观其变。

309
00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.370
I hear you.
我懂你的意思。

310
00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:31.530
I also do want it.
我也确实想要那样。

311
00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.150
So I'm a little Dwight here.
所以我现在有点像德怀特了。

312
