00:30:51.390 --> 00:30:54.110
Here's something fun I found out about the ant farm.
关于这个蚂蚁农场，我发现了一些有趣的事。

703
00:30:54.330 --> 00:30:54.610
Oh.
哦。

704
00:30:54.950 --> 00:30:59.670
The ant farm featured in this episode is an Uncle Milton ant farm.
这集里出现的蚂蚁农场是米尔顿叔叔（Uncle Milton）牌的。

705
00:30:59.930 --> 00:31:00.910
Phil Shea bought it.
是菲尔·谢伊买的。

706
00:31:01.030 --> 00:31:02.150
It cost about $23.
大概花了23美元。

707
00:31:02.150 --> 00:31:03.870
You can find them on Amazon.
你们可以在亚马逊上找到。

708
00:31:04.530 --> 00:31:11.690
But I read a great article about Milton Levine who invented this ant farm in the New York Times.
但我读过《纽约时报》上一篇关于发明这个蚂蚁农场的米尔顿·莱文（Milton Levine）的精彩文章。

709
00:31:11.910 --> 00:31:12.490
Uncle Milton?
米尔顿叔叔？

710
00:31:12.930 --> 00:31:13.530
Yes.
对。

711
00:31:13.830 --> 00:31:14.930
Milton Levine.
米尔顿·莱文。

712
00:31:15.170 --> 00:31:16.430
Here's what the article said.
文章是这么说的。

713
00:31:16.430 --> 00:31:20.690
In 1956, Milton Levine had a Eureka moment.
1956年，米尔顿·莱文灵光一现。

714
00:31:20.970 --> 00:31:27.230
He spotted a mound of ants during a Fourth of July picnic at his sister's poolside in Southern California.
他在南加州他姐姐家泳池边参加独立日野餐时，发现了一堆蚂蚁。

715
00:31:27.230 --> 00:31:32.310
Recalling as a boy how he had collected ants in jars at his uncle's farm in Pennsylvania,
他回想起小时候在宾夕法尼亚州他叔叔的农场里用罐子收集蚂蚁的情景，

716
00:31:32.670 --> 00:31:37.010
he told his brother-in-law and business partner, we should make an ant uranium.
于是他对他的姐夫兼商业伙伴说，我们应该做一个蚂蚁农场。

717
00:31:37.410 --> 00:31:43.710
The resulting product, Uncle Milton's ant farm, has been a staple in children's bedrooms ever since.
由此产生的产品——米尔顿叔叔蚂蚁农场，从此成了孩子们卧室里的常客。

718
00:31:43.710 --> 00:31:46.530
More than 20 million have been sold.
销量已经超过了2000万个。

719
00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:52.030
The thing that fascinates me about this, because as a parent, I have looked into the ant farm,
作为一个家长，我研究过这个蚂蚁农场，最让我着迷的一点是，

720
00:31:52.270 --> 00:31:57.210
is that they send you a little tube of ants.
他们会寄给你一小管蚂蚁。

721
00:31:57.390 --> 00:31:58.450
A little vial of them.
一小瓶蚂蚁。

722
00:31:58.610 --> 00:31:58.830
Yeah.
是啊。

723
00:31:59.110 --> 00:32:01.910
Live ants that you add to the farm.
活的蚂蚁，让你放进农场里。

724
00:32:01.910 --> 00:32:10.170
But how many times, Angela, do you think that the transfer from the tube to the house has gone awry?
但安吉拉，你觉得从管子转移到农场里这个过程，出过多少次岔子？

725
00:32:10.250 --> 00:32:10.590
I know.
我知道。

726
00:32:11.230 --> 00:32:12.750
I'm sure I'm going to say this wrong.
我肯定会读错这个词。

727
00:32:13.050 --> 00:32:14.930
I'm positive I am.
我敢肯定。

728
00:32:15.050 --> 00:32:22.310
But the type of ants that are in the ant farm are Paganomarex californicus, red ants from California.
但蚂蚁农场里的蚂蚁品种是Paganomarex californicus，一种来自加州的红蚂蚁。

729
00:32:22.690 --> 00:32:25.850
Oh, just like the ones he saw in the little mound by the pool.
哦，就像他在泳池边的小土堆里看到的那种。

730
00:32:26.290 --> 00:32:29.850
Mr. Levine, he was quoted as saying this about the ants.
莱文先生曾这样评价这些蚂蚁。

731
00:32:30.030 --> 00:32:30.410
Okay.
好的。

732
00:32:31.910 --> 00:32:33.630
Just amazing feat yet, he said.
他说，这简直是了不起的壮举。

733
00:32:33.790 --> 00:32:35.730
They put three kids through college.
它们供三个孩子读完了大学。

734
00:32:36.110 --> 00:32:36.530
Aww.
哇。

735
00:32:37.570 --> 00:32:38.850
Mr. Levine passed away.
莱文先生已经去世了。

736
00:32:39.010 --> 00:32:40.630
He was 97 years old.
他享年97岁。

737
00:32:40.750 --> 00:32:47.090
And his company, the Uncle Milton Industries, was sold to Transom Capital Group for more than $20 million.
他的公司，米尔顿叔叔工业公司，以超过2000万美元的价格卖给了Transom资本集团。

738
00:32:47.730 --> 00:32:48.370
Wow.
哇。

739
00:32:48.970 --> 00:32:49.510
Wow.
哇。

740
00:32:49.610 --> 00:32:56.850
That really shows you how a little idea can turn into something that's in every kid's bedroom.
这真的向你展示了一个小点子是如何变成每个孩子卧室里的必备品的。

741
00:32:57.070 --> 00:32:57.870
Yes, Jenna.
是的，珍娜。

742
00:32:58.290 --> 00:33:01.090
Mr. Levine once said of his company's success,
莱文先生曾这样评价他公司的成功：

743
00:33:01.090 --> 00:33:05.370
Most novelties, if they last one season, it's a lot.
大多数新奇玩意儿，如果能流行一个季度，就已经很不错了。

744
00:33:05.570 --> 00:33:08.290
If they last two seasons, it's a phenomenon.
如果能流行两个季度，那就是奇迹了。

745
00:33:08.610 --> 00:33:11.510
But to last 35 years is unheard of.
但能流行35年，简直闻所未闻。

746
00:33:11.710 --> 00:33:12.490
It's true.
确实。

747
00:33:12.650 --> 00:33:13.110
I know.
我知道。

748
00:33:13.450 --> 00:33:14.790
Well, I loved that.
嗯，我很喜欢这个故事。

